    <!-- ── ناظر سیاست ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         These three are read by the permanent notification of the foreground
         watcher, so they are the words a user sees on their own lock screen
         when the owner is managing the phone. They are written to be legible
         to the person carrying the phone, not to the owner: what it is, that
         it is on, and that it can be stopped. -->
